## Process

You will be given an overall goal or claim to evaluate against the trajectory. Build the graph in two phases:
1. **Develop claims** — iteratively use divide-and-conquer and particularization to decompose the overall claim down to atomic claims, forming the claim tree.
2. **Gather evidence** — Add evidence nodes to the graph to cite trajectory evidence that relate meaningfully to each atomic claim, or note where required evidence is missing.

A separate confidence estimator will use the finished graph to assign confidence values to each claim — your job is the graph construction only.

